    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by two integer types of different signedness. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The built-in comparison of a signed and an unsigned operand converts the signed one to the unsigned type, so <computeroutput>-1 &lt; 1u</computeroutput> is false. For these pairs the comparisons use the <computeroutput>std::cmp_*()</computeroutput> functions, which compare the mathematical values. The character types take part as the integers of the same size and signedness (see <computeroutput>comparison_integer</computeroutput>), since the built-in comparison of a signed <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> with an <computeroutput>unsigned</computeroutput>, or of a <computeroutput>char32_t</computeroutput> with an <computeroutput>int</computeroutput>, has the same problem. <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput> is excluded, since <computeroutput>std::cmp_*()</computeroutput> do not accept it and its comparison with integers is not a sign problem.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the left operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the right operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
